head=(U/'docs/Validation.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8').split('<main>')[0].replace('Milano Racing validation','Milano Racing — Venue Environment Research')
body='<main><p class="tag">MILANO RACING / ENVIRONMENT RESEARCH / 22 OCTOBER 2026</p><h1>Whole-circuit surroundings</h1><p>This is the environment inventory for all twelve circuits. The acceptance target is a continuous, recognisable setting throughout a lap: distinctive buildings, supporting neighbourhoods, terrain, vegetation, roads, bridges, shorelines, grandstands and pits. One landmark per track is not sufficient.</p><p><strong>Evidence status:</strong> geographic footprints and source IDs establish placement, not facade fidelity. Architectural meshes are reconstructions. A count of buildings or a successful load test does not prove a complete replica. The remaining accuracy work below is deliberately visible.</p>'
body+='<h2>How the environment is built</h2><ol><li>Register OSM footprints and roads to each circuit’s metre coordinate frame; retain source way/node IDs.</li><li>Use terrain elevation and mapped land cover for foundations, slopes, shorelines and forests. Satellite colour is from 2016/2017 and is not evidence of current building geometry.</li><li>Reconstruct important silhouettes and structural features from promoter, architect, fabricator and heritage sources. Detailed dimensions without a published reference remain estimates.</li><li>Check concave roofs/courtyards, bridge continuity and supports, road clearance and full-lap views. Keep moving guides and foliage out of immutable scenery batches.</li><li>Measure render cost with repeatable viewpoints and keep the same scene across quality presets. Do not substitute a landmark count for visual inspection.</li></ol>'
for ident,d in tour.items():
 scope,built,sources=venues[ident];ctx=context.get(ident,{'structures':[],'infrastructure':[]});blds=[f for f in mapped.get(ident,[]) if f['kind']=='building']
 body+=f'<section id="{ident}"><h2>{H(d["name"])}</h2><p><strong>Full-lap scope.</strong> {H(scope)}</p><p><strong>Current model.</strong> {H(built)}</p>'
 if ident!='milano':body+=f'<p class="small">Map inventory: {len(blds)} building footprint pieces; {len(ctx["structures"])} context selections; {len(ctx["infrastructure"])} connecting infrastructure records. Existing primary landmark models are additional. Some records share one physical structure and should not be counted as separate landmarks.</p>'
 frame=U/f'qa/{ident}-circuit.png'
 if frame.exists():
  images=U/'docs/inspection';images.mkdir(exist_ok=True);shutil.copy2(frame,images/frame.name)
  body+=f'<figure style="margin:20px 0"><a href="inspection/{frame.name}"><img loading="lazy" src="inspection/{frame.name}" alt="Current {H(d["name"])} game view"></a><figcaption class="small">Current in-game inspection frame. One view of the environment; not evidence that every landmark is accurately reproduced.</figcaption></figure>'
 body+='<ul>'+''.join(f'<li><a href="{H(url)}">{H(name)}</a></li>' for name,url in sources)+'</ul></section>'
body+='<h2>Remaining fidelity work</h2><p>These are game reconstructions, not laser scans. Individual facade proportions, ornament, roof plant, vegetation species and temporary race furniture still need reference matching. Monaco’s cliff/tunnel transitions, Suzuka’s other amusement rides, and season-specific street-circuit installations remain explicit follow-up items. Public OSM data has missing heights and incomplete outlines; generic geometry at those locations must not be presented as verified architecture.</p><h2>Source trail and reproducibility</h2><p>Read <code>src/venue-context-data.json</code> for each selected name, footprint, original tags, source URL, courtyard holes and roof mesh. <code>qa/venue-source-inventory.json</code> lists named structures in the cached extracts. <code>tools/venue-context.py</code> rebuilds selections and roof geometry offline; it requires Shapely 2.1 or later. The normal game build only reads the baked JSON. OSM-derived data remains attributed under ODbL; reference photographs and promoter PDFs are not redistributed in the release.</p><p>See <a href="Validation.html">Validation and limits</a> for the exact test coverage, and <a href="Circuit%20Research.html">Circuit Research</a> for geometry, widths and racing-line sources.</p></main></html>'
(U/'docs/Venue Environment Research.html').write_text(head+body,encoding='utf-8')
print('Wrote circuit-by-circuit environment research and evidence inventory.')
